    "image.report.transforms-row.tensor.1": "ToTensor maps pixels from 0–255 to 0–1, followed by ImageNet Normalize: mean=(0.485, 0.456, 0.406), std=(0.229, 0.224, 0.225).",
    "image.report.transforms-row.tensor.2": "The preset converts to a 0–1 tensor and normalizes with the same mean/std. Each image becomes a 3×224×224 tensor, as in training.",
    "image.report.normalization-explained": "Normalize applies (x − mean)/std to each R, G, B channel after scaling pixels to 0–1; normalized tensors are no longer restricted to 0–1. Constants come from pretrained weights and are not fitted on validation/test. Inputs have 3 channels and a height and width of 224 px.",
    "image.report.transforms-limits": "Augmentation creates variations during training without increasing original image counts in the split table. Final checkpoint evaluation on train also uses deterministic preprocessing, as for validation/test, to compare the train–validation gap. Cropping may remove important scene content and upsampling adds no detail; recipe changes must be evaluated using validation.",
